# Age 3 from the completed age-2 line (Step063 play session).
#
# This file is exactly age2.jsonl (its header still explains the age-1 arc and
# the age-2 balance: 2 food sold/tick, 7 farms + 10 wells for 20 colonists)
# plus the push to the Age of Prosperity.
#
# The age-3 milestone set is pop 20, treasury 1500, 30 operational buildings,
# 20 residences and 3 workshops. At t=860 the line already has pop 20, 20
# residences and 891 money (+5/tick), so the only gaps are money, workshops
# and the operational count. Measured decisions:
#   1. A WORKSHOP pays its keep unstaffed: commerce is staffing-independent
#      (2 + 1 per tradeRoutes), so a third workshop adds +3/tick for 1 upkeep
#      even with every worker already placed. It is the cheapest revenue.
#   2. Residences are upkeep-exempt (Step021): 4 of them add operational
#      buildings, raise housing to 24 and cost nothing per tick.
#   3. One farm (+3 food) and two wells (+4 water) carry the growth from 20
#      to 24: 8 farms = 25 food (24 eaten + 1 sold) and 12 wells = 24 water
#      = 24 served. The granary settles on the Step062 safety stock (24) —
#      a food balance of 0 that no longer starves anyone.
#   4. Do NOT add a fourth workshop: each one pollutes, and 4 workshops put
#      pollution at 100 with only 2 parks, closing admission and starving the
#      colony (measured: pop 22/24, food 0, verdict CRITICAL). Three is enough
#      because the operational count already clears 30 with the extra farm/wells.
# Measured: HEALTHY at t=1100 with pop 24/24, money 2441 (net +7/tick),
# age-2 milestones all done, 0 rejected command; advanceAge then opens
# Age 3 with its own set already satisfied.
# Age 2 from the shipped opening (Step061 play session).
#
# Lines 1-25 are exactly balanced.jsonl (the age-1 arc: cropRotation, parks
# before growth, water before housing, purchases spread) and end at t=660 with
# pop 16/16, pollution 0, money 587, net +3/tick, verdict HEALTHY.
#
# Everything after that was measured, and two measurements changed the plan:
#   1. tech3 — the pending age-1 milestone is "3 technologies"; masonry and
#      tradeRoutes (50$ each) are the only age-1 techs left. tradeRoutes is no
#      filler: +1 commerce per connected workshop, 4 -> 6 /tick.
#   2. advanceAge — pop 16 >= 8, 34 buildings >= 8, treasury >= 200, 3 techs.
#   3. market1 needs 2 PLANKS and the colony owns none, so the milestone runs
#      through real industry: a lumber camp on the (4,4) wood deposit feeds the
#      two existing workshops. `plan` proved the ORDER matters — 15 jobs for 16
#      colonists leaves exactly one spare worker, so the camp is staffed only if
#      built BEFORE the extra workshops (staffing is positional, y then x: a
#      row-3 shop is hired before a row-4 camp and would take that worker).
#      Measured: 36 wood mined in 20 ticks -> 18 planks, ~+10 money/tick.
#   4. A market sells 2 food/tick from the granary but never below one tick of
#      consumption (Step062 safety stock: trade drains the buffer, never the
#      next meal). A food balance of 0 is therefore survivable — the granary
#      just settles on its floor and the market stops earning. Producing
#      EXACTLY (mouths + 2) is what keeps the granary level AND the 2
#      money/tick; more fills the granary and wastes the overflow (the
#      "storage full" warning is a critical verdict).
#   5. Water must match too: 2 water per well, so the population has to be even.
#      With irrigation (4/farm) five farms give 21 = 19 mouths + 2 sold, and 19
#      is odd — no well count reaches it (measured: 10 wells at pop 19 wasted
#      +1 water/tick, verdict CRITICAL). Without irrigation seven farms give
#      7*3 + 1 anchor = 22 = 20 mouths + 2 sold, and 10 wells = 20 exactly.
#      Irrigation is therefore NOT researched here; the fifth tech is wheelbarrow.
# 20 ticks after the last build the state is an exact balance, not a happy
# accident: food 22 produced = 20 eaten + 2 sold, water 20 = 20, jobs 20 = 20
# workers, pollution 0 with 2 parks against 2 workshops.
{"cmd":"init"}
{"cmd":"tick","n":120}
{"cmd":"do","command":{"kind":"researchTech","techId":"cropRotation"}}
{"cmd":"build","type":"park","x":11,"y":1}
{"cmd":"build","type":"park","x":15,"y":1}
{"cmd":"tick","n":300}
{"cmd":"report"}
{"cmd":"do","command":{"kind":"placeRoads","cells":["19,2","21,2"]}}
{"cmd":"build","type":"well","x":18,"y":2,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"well","x":20,"y":2,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"well","x":22,"y":2,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"residence","x":13,"y":1,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"residence","x":17,"y":1,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"residence","x":19,"y":1,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"residence","x":21,"y":1,"road":false}
{"cmd":"tick","n":60}
{"cmd":"report"}
{"cmd":"build","type":"residence","x":23,"y":1,"road":false}
{"cmd":"build","type":"residence","x":12,"y":2,"road":false}
{"cmd":"tick","n":60}
{"cmd":"assess"}
{"cmd":"tick","n":120}
{"cmd":"assess"}
# --- age-1 milestones close, age 2 opens ---
{"cmd":"do","command":{"kind":"researchTech","techId":"masonry"}}
{"cmd":"do","command":{"kind":"researchTech","techId":"tradeRoutes"}}
{"cmd":"do","command":{"kind":"advanceAge"}}
